seg-090bf5ae96b6 = <b>GNSS beyond the constellation (<c1/>).</b> A new scenario kind for spacecraft above, around and past the GNSS orbits (<a1><c2/></a1>): availability of one and four signals, outage durations, C/N0, DOP and main-lobe against sidelobe links for GPS, GLONASS, Galileo, BDS, QZSS and NavIC on a shell or along LEO, MEO, GEO, HEO and lunar-transfer trajectories; booklet, parametric or user-supplied transmit patterns; a limb-ray ionosphere, plasmasphere and atmosphere model; a weak-signal receiver design; an onboard GNSS extended Kalman filter for HEO and lunar transfer; and formation relative navigation. Compared with the ICG Space Service Volume booklet under a pre-registration committed before the run: the minimum-radiated-power constants and the lunar bar agree, the other bars are not met under the pre-registered reading (almost all through the booklet's inconsistent GLONASS beam angle), and the parametric sidelobe stand-in does not reproduce the measured GPS panel patterns. Everything stays MODELLED (<a2><c3/></a2>).

