seg-9889575c2df1 = <b><c1/> and <c2/>: signed, verifiable evidence packs for a GNSS trust event.</b> A pack bundles the raw log slice and the full log's SHA-256, the configuration with every threshold, the per-epoch results and reasons, the engine version, a hash-chained manifest and a self-contained HTML summary, signed with Ed25519 (a key from <c3/> or your own file; keys are never stored in a pack and <c4/> is git-ignored). <c5/> checks every hash, the chain and the signature and names exactly what fails; with <c6/> it pins the signer. An RFC { "3161" } token can be attached and is read and bound to the manifest (the authority's own signature is not checked by this build; <c7/> covers it). The log slice is the window's exact bytes where the reader reports source spans (NMEA, UBX, RINEX { "3" }, Android), otherwise the whole log, and the manifest says which. Creation and verification are pure public functions (<c8/>) that build for <c9/>. The packs state that they are a technical record, not a legal opinion. The new dependencies are the <c10/> tree (BSD-3-Clause and Apache-2.0/MIT, minimal features) and a direct <c11/> (already in that tree) to wipe key material. See <c12/>.

