seg-1c88bffc605b = <b>GNSS IQ layer on the CLI and Python ({ "0.32.0" } Phase A).</b> The existing <c1/> module is now usable without writing Rust. Five new <c2/> commands join the data-handling group: <c3/> generates a long multi-satellite IQ scene to a file with a truth sidecar; <c4/> runs FFT acquisition of one or more PRNs over a recording and reports each detection (PRN, Doppler, code phase, statistic, threshold); <c5/> acquires then runs the DLL/PLL/FLL bank over a recording and emits per-epoch tracking output (CSV/JSON) with configurable loop bandwidths, integration time and correlator spacing; <c6/> replays one recording across several loop designs and reports the resulting jitter and lock metrics per design; and <c7/> fits the tracking-loop loss-of-lock model to a receiver-trust timeline. The same core is exposed to Python (<c8/>, <c9/>, <c10/>, <c11/>, <c12/>), returning NumPy-friendly lists and dicts. Software-only and additive: no new dependencies, no transmit, no interference or spoofing waveform synthesis; the engine, acquisition, tracking and loop designs are the crate's own, so a CLI or Python caller gets the same bits as the Rust tests. New module <c13/>; the scene's own truth sidecar is the independent oracle in <c14/> (acquisition recovers each injected code phase and Doppler, tracking converges to the injected Doppler). No published scenario-kind count or verification-matrix row changes.

