seg-e70cc0973fa3 = <b>Eccentric orbits and J2 drift.</b> The orbit type is now a full Keplerian orbit (semi-major axis, eccentricity, inclination, RAAN, argument of perigee, mean anomaly), propagated by solving Kepler's equation, with optional secular J2 nodal regression and apsidal precession. New optional <c1/>, <c2/>, and <c3/> scenario fields, and an <c4/> reference scenario (a { "12" } h highly-eccentric critically-inclined user). Circular orbits keep the original closed-form path bit-for-bit.

# text
seg-cc041e16d418 = The hybrid (combined-PNT) pack now reports <b>Integrity</b> and <b>Security</b>, so all four packs cover the full set of operational figures of merit. Integrity is the timing-channel protection-bound containment from a Kalman estimator disciplined to truth while GNSS is nominal and re-anchored (more loosely) at each optical re-sync; its bound includes the link's measurement-noise floor, so a clock far better than the link is scored against the delivered solution's actual noise. Security is the clock-aided spoof-detection score against the timing spec.

# text
# c1: scripts/changelog-extract.sh
seg-e0b666457d6e = Release notes are now generated from the curated CHANGELOG section for the tag (<c1/>), so each GitHub release highlights what changed instead of listing raw commits.

