# c2: q_arw
seg-5b7fcd386fd3 = Gyro channel for the inertial model: residual gyro bias and angular random walk drive an attitude (tilt) error that couples gravity into a horizontal specific-force error, the dominant strapdown error-growth mechanism. Off by default; enabled per sensor via the optional <c1/> and <c2/> fields.

# text
# c1: q_wf*T + q_rw*T^3/3
seg-efe9f10d2641 = Two-state (phase, frequency) Kalman clock estimator with exact van Loan process-noise discretisation. Coasting from a known state reproduces the analytic holdover error growth (<c1/>) exactly, and the filter additionally yields an online 1-sigma uncertainty bound.

# text
seg-539e24f34ed1 = The clock run now reports the <b>Integrity</b> figure of merit (previously unpopulated): the fraction of outage samples whose error stays inside the filter's 3-sigma protection bound, surfaced in the JSON result and CLI summary.

